  "overview": {
    "text": "A baseball home run (HR, or “homer”) is a fair-ball play on which the batter scores without being put out or benefiting from an error. Most often, the ball flies over the outfield fence in fair territory: the batter is credited with all four bases, and any runners already on base score as well. A ball that hits a foul pole counts. The ball need not leave the field, however: when it stays in play and the batter safely touches all four bases, it is an inside-the-park home run. Because one swing can score several runs, homers can sharply affect a game; they are also used to gauge hitting power, although park dimensions and conditions influence totals.",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://www.mlb.com/glossary/standard-stats/home-run"
    ]
  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "text": "A home run hit over the fence in fair territory gives the batter all four bases and scores any runners already on base.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mlb.com/glossary/standard-stats/home-run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A ball that hits a foul pole is a home run; foul poles mark the boundary between fair and foul territory.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mlb.com/glossary/standard-stats/home-run",
        "https://content.mlb.com/documents/2/2/4/305750224/2019_Official_Baseball_Rules_FINAL_.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "An inside-the-park home run happens when a batter keeps the ball in play but safely reaches all four bases without being put out.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mlb.com/glossary/standard-stats/home-run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Home runs are used to evaluate hitters’ power, but ballpark size, wall height, and wind can affect whether a hit clears the fence.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.mlb.com/glossary/standard-stats/home-run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Home-run records have been celebrated milestones: the Baseball Hall of Fame describes Babe Ruth’s 60 home runs in 1927 as a major benchmark, while noting that later players surpassed it.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://baseballhall.org/discover/short-stops/babe-ruths-60th-home-run-ball"
      ]
    }
  ],
